The Iron Man Mark XLIV (44) suit, universally known as the "Hulkbuster," made its massive screen debut in Avengers: Age of Ultron as a joint countermeasure designed by Tony Stark and Bruce Banner in case the Hulk ever lost control. Standing over eleven feet tall and weighing several tons, the suit is deployed from "Veronica," an orbital platform satellite that drops heavy exo-frame modules directly over Tony's base Mark 43 armor to lock him inside a heavy-duty exoskeleton. Powered by multiple Arc Reactors distributed across its body, the Hulkbuster features extreme structural plating, hydraulic jackhammer fists, pneumatic grappling clamps, high-potency chemical sedatives, and a surrounding cage of replacement parts continuously launched from Veronica to repair damaged limbs mid-combat during his destructive showdown with an enraged Hulk in Johannesburg.
